[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Scandinavian Defense"]
[Variation "Scandinavian Defense: Valencian Variation"]
[ECO "B01"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "bishop-pair,h3-bishop-question"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...Qd8"]
[Start "qa5-classical 3.Nc3"]

3... Qd8 4. d4 Nf6 ( 4... c6 5. Nf3 Nf6 6. h3 ) ( 4... Bf5 5. Nf3 e6 6. Bd3 { Offers to trade Black's best minor piece, the bishop that got out before ...e6. } 6... Bxd3 7. Qxd3 Nf6 { The same position as 4...Nf6 5.Nf3 Bf5 6.Bd3 Bxd3 7.Qxd3 e6. } ) ( 4... Nc6 5. d5 { Gains space and hits the knight, which has no good square in the centre. } 5... Nb8 ( 5... Ne5 6. Bf4 { Develops with an attack on the knight, which must move again. } 6... Ng6 7. Bg3 ) ( 5... Nb4 6. a3 { Kicks the knight away before it can jump to c2. } 6... Na6 7. Bf4 ) 6. Bf4 { Develops and keeps the extra space. Black has spent three moves on the queen and knight and is behind. } ) 5. Nf3 Bg4 ( 5... e6 { Shuts in the c8 bishop. The same position as 4...e6 5.Nf3 Nf6, where White plays Bd3. } ) ( 5... Nc6 6. Bb5 { Pins the knight to the king, so it cannot jump to b4 or attack d4 freely. } 6... e6 7. O-O { Castles. Plan: Re1 and Ne5, or Bxc6 to give Black doubled pawns. } ) ( 5... Bf5 6. Bd3 { Offers to trade bishops. Black's bishop is the piece that would otherwise be shut in by ...e6. } 6... Bxd3 7. Qxd3 e6 8. O-O { Castles. White's queen and knights are active, and Black has no good pawn break. } ) ( 5... g6 6. Bc4 { Points the bishop at f7 and keeps g5 and f4 free for the other bishop. } 6... Bg7 7. O-O O-O 8. Re1 { Puts the rook on the open e-file. Plan: Bf4 or Bg5 and Qd2, aiming at Black's king. } ) 6. h3 { Asks the bishop what it wants. Taking on f3 hands White the bishop pair; going to h5 lets g4 trap it later. } 6... Bxf3 ( 6... Bh5 7. g4 { The pawn covers f5 and attacks the bishop, so it can only go to g6. } 7... Bg6 8. Ne5 { Eyes g6 and prepares h4-h5, which hits the bishop. It has no good retreat, so Black ends up trading it off. [%cal Gh2h4] } ) 7. Qxf3 { Takes back with the queen, which is now active and eyes b7. } 7... c6 8. Be3 { Guards d4 so the queen can stay on f3, and develops the last minor piece. } 8... e6 9. Bd3 Nbd7 10. O-O-O { Castles long so the king is safe and the rook looks down the d-file. Plan: g4 and g5 to drive the knight away, with the bishop pair behind the pawns. } *
